Share mapped members without broad rebuilding

Carry monotone element maps through keys and child prefix trees so
native transport can share entire inherited relation subtrees. Cache
transformed children on demand and filter empty images. Shared transform
descriptors keep ordinary data nodes small and let edited paths retain
untouched mapped child views and immutable snapshots.

Keep sparse updates and comparisons driven by the few changed keys.
Normalize small mapped sets without scanning their entire cardinality.
Build general image sets in place, preserving empty-result sharing,
and use sorted keys for any full-level rebuild that is still needed.
Merge singleton suffixes through mutable entries so late images reuse
destination paths while empty destinations retain subtree sharing.
Reuse target coverage across owned-support cleanup when a single model
prefix identifies the same immutable target slice for both checks.
Carry source keys alongside deferred value lookups so the common single
transform needs no temporary allocation or repeated key conversions.

Represent contiguous leaf elements as shared intervals while keeping
scattered sets in trees. Keep fragmented intervals in persistent trees
so sparse holes never expand every surviving member into a node.
Compare shared interval subtrees directly and retain covered roots in
unions and intersections, avoiding repeated work after equality.

Preserve canonical current rows, historical snapshots, and bounded
work accounting through equality and updates. Charge interval traversal
separately from member expansion while retaining cheap dense-leaf work.
Keep balancing ratios valid even when physical size bounds are large.
Resolve and release deep mapping chains iteratively so evaluator
threads with small stacks can edit and destroy mapped snapshots.

Validation covers mapped edits, filtered pivots, partial and conflicting
images, composition, random set operations, source and owner equality,
dynamic roundtrips, and finite fuel. Native and desugared generated
models retain the same results under both evaluation strategies.

Retain raw cache origins through identity and uniform-offset views so
value lookups avoid repeatedly searching the same morphism chain. Keep
proper subtree origins small and compose validated offsets modulo the ID
width while preserving filtered domains and historical snapshots.

Seek through partial mapping domains without visiting excluded source
rows. Preserve each child's bounds while returning to ordinary sibling
paths, and keep exact trees on a direct iterator path. Avoid repeated
endpoint searches when outer bounds already cover a complete map image.

Map bounded materialized suffixes directly to avoid deferred caches for
just a few entries. Preflight rejects existing lazy descendants without
evaluating their callbacks, so a small parent cannot force a large
suffix emptiness check. Keep point adapters outside range iterator
storage so ordinary leaf traversal needs less stack space.

Reuse owned destination suffixes during bulk unions. For colliding
non-injective head images, extend the existing child directly instead
of building and discarding an intermediate suffix. Multiple images
still share a transformed child, and filtering keeps snapshots intact.

Keep mapped seeking outside the ordinary iterator's inlining budget so
full tuple consumption retains a compact range traversal loop.

Use a surviving materialized pivot to answer emptiness checks without
forcing deferred descendants after a path edit.
